-- An interface default body is SPECIALIZED into every impl that does not override
-- it (desugar's fillImplDefaults).  Each specialization must reach its OWN route
-- cell: the cells on `EBinOp`/`EUnOp`/`ENumLit` are stamped from the grounded
-- operand type, so one cell shared by N specializations lets whichever impl
-- grounds first decide codegen for all of them.  With `RScalar "Int"` in the tree
-- (#2356 ground Int comparison), a single `impl Keyed Int` anywhere in the graph
-- compiled every other impl's `<` to an `icmp` over BOXED pointers — silently
-- wrong, no error.
--
-- The shape is load-bearing: it must be an interface DEFAULT METHOD.  A plain
-- polymorphic binding pins nothing here — its `<` never grounds, so it stays on
-- `@mdk_value_lt` whether or not the cells are shared.
--
-- The three impls are the three scalar dispositions the emitter distinguishes:
-- Float (inline `load double` + `fcmp`), String (`@mdk_string_compare_raw`), Int
-- (inline `icmp slt` on the tagged words).  The Int arm is half the property —
-- separating the cells must not COST Int its witness, only stop it from being
-- spent on the others.
--
--   b0 ordered 1.5 2.5 = True  -> 1     b3 ordered "b" "a" = False -> 0
--   b1 ordered 2.5 1.5 = False -> 0     b4 ordered 1   2   = True  -> 16
--   b2 ordered "a" "b" = True  -> 4     b5 ordered 2   1   = False -> 0
--
-- main = 1 + 4 + 16 = 21.  A poisoned Float or String body moves the low bits; a
-- withdrawn Int witness leaves the value at 21 but moves the .ll golden.

interface Keyed a requires Ord a where
  keyOf : a -> a
  ordered : a -> a -> Bool
  ordered x y = keyOf x < keyOf y

impl Keyed Float where
  keyOf f = f

impl Keyed String where
  keyOf s = s

impl Keyed Int where
  keyOf x = x

bit : Bool -> Int
bit b = if b then 1 else 0

main : Int
main =
  bit (ordered 1.5 2.5)
    + 2 * bit (ordered 2.5 1.5)
    + 4 * bit (ordered "a" "b")
    + 8 * bit (ordered "b" "a")
    + 16 * bit (ordered 1 2)
    + 32 * bit (ordered 2 1)
